1
00:01:06,739 --> 00:01:09,033
Thank you, Detective

2
00:01:17,625 --> 00:01:19,710
Any change?
Nothing since you left.

3
00:01:27,510 --> 00:01:30,137
She seems to be looking for something.

4
00:01:30,554 --> 00:01:30,846
Camera?

5
00:01:59,166 --> 00:02:00,626
She has a nice ass.

6
00:02:02,628 --> 00:02:04,630
Stay focused on the mission.

7
00:02:11,887 --> 00:02:14,807
Keep an eye on her, but don't get too close.

8
00:02:25,943 --> 00:02:28,154
- Good morning
- Good morning

9
00:02:28,529 --> 00:02:29,363
What can I get for you?

10
00:02:29,822 --> 00:02:31,323
Tea with milk and fresh orange juice-

11
00:02:31,699 --> 00:02:33,993
-and a croissant with butter, I've already attended to it.

12
00:02:34,827 --> 00:02:36,412
- Thank you
- No problem.

13
00:02:42,877 --> 00:02:46,797
- Do you have a visual?
- I've got visual, she's drinking her tea.

14
00:02:48,049 --> 00:02:48,507
- Say again?
- She's drinking her tea!

15
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:53,971
- Can I get you a tea, sir?
- No, no thank you.

16
00:03:08,903 --> 00:03:10,738
- Good morning, sir
- Good morning

17
00:03:11,030 --> 00:03:13,699
- I'm looking for Elise Ward
- Ward, the lady (pointing)

18
00:03:15,284 --> 00:03:15,659
Okay, thanks

19
00:03:18,788 --> 00:03:21,582
- Good morning, Elise Ward?
- Yes, that's me.

20
00:03:21,999 --> 00:03:23,167
I have a letter for you

21
00:03:23,459 --> 00:03:24,502
She's talking to someone

22
00:03:24,794 --> 00:03:26,087
A delivery boy

23
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:34,553
Scotland Yard, London

24
00:03:36,555 --> 00:03:37,640
Yes?

25
00:03:38,265 --> 00:03:43,187
She's at the usual cafe, she's speaking with a man,
it looks like a messenger...

26
00:03:43,521 --> 00:03:46,190
But you said to call if anything changed in her routine

27
00:03:50,945 --> 00:03:53,489
Stay on his face.  His face!

28
00:03:59,245 --> 00:04:03,749
- Do you think it's Alexander Pierce?
- I think everybody's Pierce.

29
00:04:05,292 --> 00:04:07,336
No, it's okay.
It is a gift, you can keep it.

30
00:04:08,129 --> 00:04:08,796
Thank you

31
00:04:24,603 --> 00:04:25,187
- Here you go, goodbye.
- Goodbye.

32
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:25,187
Get him.

33
00:04:25,604 --> 00:04:26,188
Alright, grab him.

34
00:04:28,941 --> 00:04:30,317
Let's move.

35
00:04:30,943 --> 00:04:33,487
Sir, sir! Sir, we are police.

36
00:04:35,322 --> 00:04:38,034
- What did I do?
- You're under arrest

37
00:04:38,617 --> 00:04:41,829
- You're coming with us.
- What did I do? - Shh!

38
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:44,415
What are you arresting me for?

39
00:04:57,470 --> 00:05:01,390
"Elise, you have no reason to trust me any more..."

40
00:05:01,932 --> 00:05:03,601
"But give me a chance to explain myself"

41
00:05:03,851 --> 00:05:07,313
"I know the police are watching you, we have to throw them off the trail"

42
00:05:08,397 --> 00:05:11,067
"Board the 8:22 at the Gare De Lyon"

43
00:05:11,942 --> 00:05:15,237
"Pick someone my height and build, and make them believe it is me"

44
00:05:22,995 --> 00:05:24,413
"Burn this letter."

45
00:05:25,081 --> 00:05:31,212
"It is important you follow my instructions precisely.
I love you, Alexander"

46
00:05:35,466 --> 00:05:36,717
It's from him.

47
00:05:52,775 --> 00:05:55,403
Save that letter, go in now.
Save that letter!

48
00:05:55,611 --> 00:05:56,737
Go, now!

49
00:06:07,581 --> 00:06:10,167
- No, stop! Police!
- What happened?

50
00:06:12,211 --> 00:06:13,587
Well?

51
00:06:15,047 --> 00:06:17,383
The letter is burned to shit.

52
00:06:18,718 --> 00:06:20,469
Don't fucking touch it.

53
00:06:21,178 --> 00:06:24,765
Collect the ashes, take them to the van.
I'll send you someone.

54
00:06:49,081 --> 00:06:51,667
The road's too narrow, we have to go around.  Quick!

55
00:07:02,386 --> 00:07:06,974
Turn right!
Quick, go!

56
00:07:35,086 --> 00:07:35,920
Let's go

57
00:07:46,097 --> 00:07:51,227
Police, make way!

58
00:07:58,859 --> 00:08:00,069
Damn!

59
00:08:09,829 --> 00:08:11,580
Scotland Yard

60
00:08:16,752 --> 00:08:18,004
Wednesday meeting.

61
00:08:26,971 --> 00:08:31,183
So, Alexander Pierce has a new face
Just as you suspected

62
00:08:32,893 --> 00:08:37,064
I'd have thought it must've taken quite a lot of the
money he stole from Reginald Shaw

63
00:08:37,648 --> 00:08:40,693
To finance this transformation

64
00:08:41,819 --> 00:08:46,240
Ahmed Toubali, bicycle courier of Algerian descent

65
00:08:47,074 --> 00:08:50,995
Not only has Pierce acquired a wife, and a child...

66
00:08:51,871 --> 00:08:55,875
He is also 4 inches shorter than the used to be.

67
00:08:56,167 --> 00:08:58,461
That must have been a big item of expenditure?

68
00:09:01,213 --> 00:09:04,925
Congratulations Acheson,
You have indeed cracked this case.

69
00:09:10,348 --> 00:09:14,727
Sir, this morning she recieved a note...
and we have strong reason to believe -

70
00:09:14,935 --> 00:09:20,274
Alexander Pierce has 744 million in illegal assets

71
00:09:20,566 --> 00:09:23,527
That given he is a British Subject, we might seize.

72
00:09:23,861 --> 00:09:29,033
This operation so far has cost me
eight million pounds.

73
00:09:29,033 --> 00:09:33,162
If I thought there were more than a one in a hundred
chance you could be successful...

74
00:09:33,496 --> 00:09:36,665
It would be rational for me to continue this operation...

75
00:09:38,918 --> 00:09:40,294
I do not.

76
00:09:44,965 --> 00:09:47,802
... that's an amendment... yes...

77
00:09:55,726 --> 00:09:56,936
Thank you, sir

78
00:11:00,958 --> 00:11:02,293
8:22

79
00:11:04,295 --> 00:11:07,465
- Sir, the projection for the faces you asked for
- Not now

80
00:11:10,051 --> 00:11:12,636
"8:22 Lyon"

81
00:11:14,096 --> 00:11:17,183
Are they meeting in Lyon at eight twenty-two?

82
00:11:17,475 --> 00:11:20,311
- Gare de Lyon, perhaps?
- Gare de Lyon...

83
00:11:26,692 --> 00:11:30,613
That's it, Gare De Lyon!
The train station, she's getting on a 8:22 train.

84
00:11:30,946 --> 00:11:31,655
Go!

85
00:11:38,996 --> 00:11:41,749
"Board the 8:22 at the Gare De Lyon"

86
00:11:57,598 --> 00:12:00,685
"Pick someone my height and build, and make them believe it is me"

87
00:13:11,964 --> 00:13:14,467
- I'm sorry
- What for?

88
00:13:28,939 --> 00:13:32,193
Do you mind me smoking?
It's not a real cigarette.

89
00:13:32,193 --> 00:13:34,278
- What?
- It's electronic

90
00:13:34,278 --> 00:13:39,575
It delivers the same amount of nicotine, but the smoke is water vapor.
Yeah, watch! (puffs)

91
00:13:40,993 --> 00:13:42,244
LED light

92
00:13:44,372 --> 00:13:46,374
That's somewhat disappointing.

93
00:13:48,501 --> 00:13:50,252
Would you rather have me smoking for real?

94
00:13:50,252 --> 00:13:53,297
No, I would rather you be a man who did exactly as he pleased.

95
00:13:56,175 --> 00:13:58,803
- I'm Elise
- I'm Frank

96
00:13:58,803 --> 00:14:02,723
- That's a terrible name
- (laughs) Yeah, that's the only one I've got.

97
00:14:04,308 --> 00:14:06,977
- Maybe we can find you another...
- Okay

98
00:14:12,149 --> 00:14:18,906
- You're British  - Mmm
- I'm American  - Hmm

99
00:14:22,118 --> 00:14:23,869
What brings you to Venice?

100
00:14:24,954 --> 00:14:28,582
You read spy novels.
I am a mysterious woman on a train..

101
00:14:29,291 --> 00:14:31,877
You tell me what my story is.

102
00:14:33,421 --> 00:14:34,380
Okay...

103
00:14:38,134 --> 00:14:42,388
I think you would be a diplomat attach?

104
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:47,810
Or maybe a girl from East Germany
whose father's been kidnapped

105
00:14:48,978 --> 00:14:52,481
And they're blackmailing you into stealing something for them...

106
00:14:52,481 --> 00:14:55,317
Probably microfilm, there's usually microfilm involved.

107
00:14:55,317 --> 00:14:58,029
- What awaits me?
- Trouble, certainly

108
00:14:58,029 --> 00:14:59,989
- Danger?
- Oh, yeah.

109
00:14:59,989 --> 00:15:02,783
You'll most likely be shot at in less than two chapters!

110
00:15:06,537 --> 00:15:08,247
Is there a man in my life?

111
00:15:11,792 --> 00:15:13,085
... have to wait and see.

112
00:15:15,338 --> 00:15:17,173
- Invite me to dinner Frank
- What?

113
00:15:21,093 --> 00:15:26,057
- Would you like to have the dinner?
- Women don't like questions

114
00:15:29,727 --> 00:15:32,104
- Join me for dinner
- Too demanding

115
00:15:33,939 --> 00:15:36,817
- Join me for dinner?
- Another question

116
00:15:41,364 --> 00:15:46,202
I'm having dinner...
If you'd care to join me

117
00:16:05,763 --> 00:16:06,972
Musician?

118
00:16:11,018 --> 00:16:12,228
Bartender?

119
00:16:17,983 --> 00:16:18,818
I give up.

120
00:16:20,486 --> 00:16:23,197
Math, I teach maths.

121
00:16:24,699 --> 00:16:27,535
I would not have guessed that.

122
00:16:27,993 --> 00:16:30,496
I'd imagine you're a cool math teacher, though?

123
00:16:30,955 --> 00:16:32,748
Still a math teacher.

124
00:16:46,721 --> 00:16:51,559
- Can I take your picture?
- Sure

125
00:17:12,955 --> 00:17:16,292
Urgent Message From:
Unit 17 To: John Acheson

126
00:17:36,479 --> 00:17:39,482
- Could this be Pierce?
- We're still working on that

127
00:17:43,361 --> 00:17:46,739
Well, I only have the sketches to go by, so...

128
00:17:48,491 --> 00:17:52,286
Ectomorpheus, same basic phenotype

129
00:17:54,246 --> 00:17:57,041
- Bottom line, could be him
- I knew we couldn't leave her

130
00:17:57,583 --> 00:18:01,253
Run a worldwide blind check on that face,
Bet you ten quid there's no match

131
00:18:01,879 --> 00:18:04,799
Okay, but what case number do you want to book it under?

132
00:18:06,759 --> 00:18:09,887
- Just run it
- Do you really think it's Pierce?

133
00:18:10,596 --> 00:18:11,597
Run it.

134
00:18:20,773 --> 00:18:22,692
Get me Italian Interpol.

135
00:18:35,162 --> 00:18:41,252
I have a strange feeling that those two people
over there are watching us

136
00:18:49,802 --> 00:18:53,639
Do you know something?
I think you're right

137
00:18:54,682 --> 00:18:55,891
Really?

138
00:19:01,522 --> 00:19:03,566
You're paranoid, math teacher

139
00:19:14,410 --> 00:19:15,411
Memorize this face

140
00:19:16,537 --> 00:19:19,957
The train arrives in 10 minutes
Stop him when he descends.

141
00:19:38,809 --> 00:19:42,688
So, what are you doing all alone in the city of lovers?

142
00:19:44,190 --> 00:19:45,733
Is there no one in your life?

143
00:19:48,319 --> 00:19:52,448
- There was.
- What happened?

144
00:19:58,454 --> 00:20:02,541
- She left me.
- I'm sorry to hear that, Frank

145
00:20:16,889 --> 00:20:22,061
"Arrival at train station Venicia Santa Lucia in 10 minutes.
End of the line"

146
00:20:23,187 --> 00:20:25,773
Guess I should go get my suitcase and stuff.

147
00:20:29,652 --> 00:20:35,324
- Goodbye
- Goodbye, thank you.

148
00:21:10,026 --> 00:21:11,402
Oh shit.

149
00:21:25,541 --> 00:21:27,168
- Sir
- Wait

150
00:21:29,837 --> 00:21:31,464
"Pick someone my height and build"

151
00:21:34,633 --> 00:21:36,761
"And make them believe it's me"

152
00:21:39,930 --> 00:21:42,058
We did get an exact match

153
00:21:42,433 --> 00:21:45,269
He's a math teacher at Madson Community College

154
00:21:45,269 --> 00:21:47,063
Frank Tupelo

155
00:21:47,855 --> 00:21:50,191
Lost his wife in a car crash three years ago

156
00:21:50,524 --> 00:21:51,817
He's a tourist

157
00:21:55,071 --> 00:21:56,072
Thank you

158
00:22:09,251 --> 00:22:10,670
Get me Italian Interpol

159
00:22:26,227 --> 00:22:27,978
Yes?

160
00:22:30,481 --> 00:22:31,315
Received

161
00:22:37,363 --> 00:22:40,324
Abort.  We go back to HQ quickly.

162
00:22:41,951 --> 00:22:42,993
On the other side.

163
00:23:28,831 --> 00:23:32,501
- What are you doing?
- The Internet Fraud Report

164
00:23:36,297 --> 00:23:39,633
So, this is what Alexander Pierce looks like?

165
00:23:40,259 --> 00:23:42,720
It's above your clearance.
Get back to your work.

166
00:24:15,711 --> 00:24:19,131
He's fluttering his eyelids like a girl, that's his tell.

167
00:24:19,632 --> 00:24:21,092
Go all in.

168
00:24:24,720 --> 00:24:25,513
Damn.

169
00:24:30,976 --> 00:24:31,977
Yes?

170
00:24:32,853 --> 00:24:35,022
I have a piece of information for Mr. Shaw

171
00:24:37,400 --> 00:24:39,485
It's concerning Alexander Pierce

172
00:24:43,030 --> 00:24:45,533
Alexander Pierce has just arrived in Venice

173
00:24:46,242 --> 00:24:47,368
With her.

174
00:24:54,959 --> 00:24:56,460
- Aleri.
- Sir

175
00:24:56,836 --> 00:25:00,715
- Change of course, Venice
- Yes, sir

176
00:25:02,049 --> 00:25:04,635
Now what do I own in Venice?

177
00:25:30,786 --> 00:25:31,328
Hi

178
00:25:32,663 --> 00:25:35,583
- Do you want to come with me?
- What?

179
00:25:38,919 --> 00:25:41,380
Oh yeah, sure, I mean, I-I could use a lift, yeah.

180
00:25:42,423 --> 00:25:44,133
Thank you very - that's very kind.

181
00:26:21,921 --> 00:26:23,547
Welcome to Venice, Madam

182
00:26:25,216 --> 00:26:26,300
Bags.

183
00:26:28,886 --> 00:26:29,637
Thank you

184
00:26:32,848 --> 00:26:34,433
Oh, uh, my bags!

185
00:26:36,268 --> 00:26:37,395
Are you coming?

186
00:26:44,026 --> 00:26:44,860
Thank you (speaking spanish)

187
00:26:51,367 --> 00:26:53,452
Hello, Welcome to Hotel Danieri, Madam

188
00:26:53,744 --> 00:26:55,913
Elise Clifton-Ward, and husband

189
00:26:59,041 --> 00:27:01,085
We have arranged for you a wonderful suite...

190
00:27:04,213 --> 00:27:05,631
with bathroom and with...

191
00:27:08,384 --> 00:27:10,720
- May I have your documents, please?
- Yes

192
00:27:11,303 --> 00:27:12,138
Thank you

193
00:27:14,098 --> 00:27:18,185
It will be my pleasure to show you up personally.
Please, this way.

194
00:27:18,269 --> 00:27:18,686
Thank you

195
00:27:20,354 --> 00:27:24,316
- Enjoy your stay, sir
- Thank you

196
00:27:36,037 --> 00:27:38,998
Everything was arranged
according to the precise instructions.

197
00:27:39,498 --> 00:27:42,043
I very much hope you will not be disappointed.

198
00:27:42,043 --> 00:27:44,253
We are entering the Doches Suite

199
00:27:45,004 --> 00:27:51,177
A room that has been a home away from home for
Marcel Proust and Honor?de Balzac

200
00:27:55,723 --> 00:27:57,767
- Have a nice day, sir
- Thank you

201
00:28:05,816 --> 00:28:06,817
Make yourself at home

202
00:28:48,818 --> 00:28:51,487
This really is a very nice hotel, isn't it?

203
00:28:52,988 --> 00:28:54,990
They think of everything, don't they?

204
00:30:02,099 --> 00:30:03,434
I know he will be with her.

205
00:30:04,143 --> 00:30:08,314
They'll be staying at one of the grand hotels.
The Pretty, The Regina, The Danieli.

206
00:30:09,148 --> 00:30:11,275
I want you to keep a watch on all of them.

207
00:30:12,443 --> 00:30:14,528
You can kill the girl, but you can't kill him.

208
00:30:16,781 --> 00:30:18,949
Not until I have my money, that is.

209
00:30:20,034 --> 00:30:23,204
- Is that clear?
- Yes, sir - Let's go.

210
00:30:42,264 --> 00:30:46,018
- You're ravenous.
- Do you mean ravishing?

211
00:30:46,477 --> 00:30:47,561
...I do.

212
00:30:48,187 --> 00:30:50,898
- You're ravenous
- I am.

213
00:30:52,233 --> 00:30:52,817
Come on!

214
00:31:07,707 --> 00:31:14,296
- The, um, Skambian champagne risotto, please.
- Excellent choice, excellent.

215
00:31:20,511 --> 00:31:24,682
He didn't say that to me
Did he not like my choice?

216
00:31:25,975 --> 00:31:27,852
Your choice was excellent.

217
00:31:45,745 --> 00:31:46,662
Who is he?

218
00:31:49,540 --> 00:31:54,378
Hotels don't give gifts like that, do they?
Who is he?

219
00:31:56,339 --> 00:31:59,967
- He's someone they used to be very important to me
- Used to?

220
00:32:03,429 --> 00:32:05,014
Are you meeting him in Venice?

221
00:32:06,807 --> 00:32:07,767
I hope so.

222
00:32:10,102 --> 00:32:13,397
- Part of me hopes I don't
- Why?

223
00:32:15,816 --> 00:32:23,115
Because I don't like being told what to do.
I don't like being "summoned".

224
00:32:25,534 --> 00:32:29,288
But it felt even worse not
hearing from him for two years.

225
00:32:44,095 --> 00:32:48,391
It's the Roman god, Janus.

226
00:32:49,850 --> 00:32:51,560
My mother gave it to me when I was little.

227
00:32:52,353 --> 00:32:57,650
She wanted it to teach me that people have two sides;
a good side, a bad side...

228
00:32:57,900 --> 00:32:59,819
Past and future

229
00:33:00,778 --> 00:33:05,783
And that we must embrace both in someone we love.

230
00:33:09,245 --> 00:33:10,538
And I tried...

231
00:33:21,841 --> 00:33:22,925
What's he like?

232
00:33:26,303 --> 00:33:32,560
He's... different from anybody I know.

233
00:33:37,606 --> 00:33:39,191
Different's good.

234
00:33:42,028 --> 00:33:46,365
Where I come from the highest compliment...
that you can offer a person...

235
00:33:47,491 --> 00:33:50,995
Is to say that they're down to earth...
Grounded.

236
00:33:51,871 --> 00:33:54,623
I hate it.  Drives me nutso.

237
00:34:03,299 --> 00:34:05,718
Would you like another Americano?

238
00:34:08,054 --> 00:34:10,473
I don't know, would I?

239
00:34:13,642 --> 00:34:18,314
It really was a very nice restaurant, wasn't it?
Oh.  Very nice wine.

240
00:34:19,982 --> 00:34:27,114
I'm making us a nice little drink.
Which is very nice of me, isn't it?

241
00:34:29,533 --> 00:34:30,534
Thank you

242
00:34:31,410 --> 00:34:33,788
Were those flowers here when we checked in?

243
00:34:49,470 --> 00:34:52,598
It is an invitation to a Ball, two nights from now.

244
00:34:56,227 --> 00:34:57,269
You've been "summoned"

245
00:34:59,230 --> 00:35:00,606
It appears I have.

246
00:35:39,311 --> 00:35:41,689
May I pay you a compliment?

247
00:35:43,190 --> 00:35:45,192
Another question you need never ask.

248
00:35:48,571 --> 00:35:53,701
You are the least down to earth person I've ever met.

249
00:36:15,431 --> 00:36:19,560
It's been a long day.
I do hope the couch will be comfortable.

250
00:36:22,146 --> 00:36:22,980
Good night

251
00:39:51,439 --> 00:39:53,607
Sorry, sir. Good morning.

252
00:39:54,358 --> 00:39:57,028
My name is Guido, your waiter.

253
00:39:57,945 --> 00:40:01,574
I'm Frank.  What's this?

254
00:40:02,199 --> 00:40:03,617
It's your breakfast, sir.

255
00:40:05,536 --> 00:40:10,041
- I didn't order any.
- The lady ordered it for you, when she left

256
00:40:18,215 --> 00:40:19,425
When she left?

257
00:40:45,993 --> 00:40:47,328
Have a nice day, sir.

258
00:41:18,067 --> 00:41:21,070
- Hi.
- Alexander let's go see an old friend

259
00:41:25,324 --> 00:41:28,035
- I'm not sure he's Pierce
- The boss warned us about this

260
00:41:28,786 --> 00:41:29,286
Get him!

261
00:41:44,593 --> 00:41:47,054
- Hello, please help
- Hello, sir

262
00:41:47,471 --> 00:41:51,559
Hello, I'm in need of help there are two
men trying to break down the door

263
00:41:52,476 --> 00:41:54,729
I see, what kind of problem do you have with the door, sir?

264
00:41:55,271 --> 00:41:58,190
No, no, no, there are two men with guns trying to break in!

265
00:41:58,190 --> 00:41:59,942
Two men carrying pistols (speaking spanish)

266
00:42:00,276 --> 00:42:02,528
- Your spanish is excellent, sir
- Thank you

267
00:42:04,530 --> 00:42:05,906
- I gotta go!
- Sir?

268
00:42:09,410 --> 00:42:10,244
Americans...

269
00:42:28,012 --> 00:42:29,722
The boss wants him alive!

270
00:42:39,648 --> 00:42:40,608
She's returned.

271
00:43:03,964 --> 00:43:04,882
Get ready to intervene.

272
00:43:08,344 --> 00:43:12,181
- Yes
- Commander Acheson, two armed men are chasing the American from yesterday.

273
00:43:12,390 --> 00:43:14,809
Shots have been fired.  Request permission to intervene.

274
00:43:15,434 --> 00:43:17,228
Do you still have Elise?

275
00:43:18,854 --> 00:43:22,024
We still have a visual on Elise Ward, but the American is in imminent danger.

276
00:43:22,483 --> 00:43:26,237
You mean the mathematics teacher from Wisconsin?
I'd say not our mandate.

277
00:43:26,696 --> 00:43:28,864
Sir, this man is in real peril.

278
00:43:30,491 --> 00:43:33,452
This is exactly why she chose him, to distract us.

279
00:43:34,245 --> 00:43:35,287
Stay with her

280
00:43:35,663 --> 00:43:39,875
Do not move unless she moves.
Am I making myself crystal clear?

281
00:43:40,459 --> 00:43:42,878
Sir, they will kill him.

282
00:43:45,923 --> 00:43:47,216
Not our mandate.

283
00:44:41,020 --> 00:44:43,773
- Look at that man!
- What the hell?

284
00:44:47,610 --> 00:44:49,945
Center, send someone to the market!

285
00:44:50,821 --> 00:44:53,991
There is a nut trying to kill himself.
American, I bet.

286
00:44:55,159 --> 00:44:56,535
Stop, stop!

287
00:44:58,287 --> 00:44:59,580
Do not jump!

288
00:45:19,308 --> 00:45:21,686
- I'm so sorry
- Asshole!

289
00:45:22,228 --> 00:45:23,020
I'm sorry!

290
00:45:26,857 --> 00:45:29,235
- Stop him
- I'm sorry, sorry!

291
00:45:54,677 --> 00:45:56,387
- Answer the phone.
- Yes, sir.

292
00:46:10,609 --> 00:46:15,531
- I think you need it more than I.
- "Thank you" (speaking spanish)

293
00:46:16,282 --> 00:46:17,533
"You're welcome" (speaking spanish)

294
00:46:19,785 --> 00:46:21,120
Smoke?

295
00:46:24,832 --> 00:46:25,374
No?

296
00:46:39,847 --> 00:46:43,225
- Now, you wish to report a murder?
- No.

297
00:46:44,935 --> 00:46:46,854
Some people tried to kill me

298
00:46:47,730 --> 00:46:49,732
I was told you are reporting a murder.

299
00:46:50,149 --> 00:46:52,401
Attempted murder.

300
00:46:53,736 --> 00:46:58,824
- That's not so serious.
- No, not when you downgrade it from murder.

301
00:46:59,950 --> 00:47:02,536
But when you upgrade it from room
service, it's quite serious.

302
00:47:02,745 --> 00:47:06,832
- So is assaulting a Police Officer.
- That was an accident.

303
00:47:07,166 --> 00:47:08,668
The Officer feels differently.

304
00:47:11,629 --> 00:47:13,297
...With all due respect, sir

305
00:47:14,382 --> 00:47:17,093
...I think maybe I should be talking with someone

306
00:47:19,303 --> 00:47:22,598
...Someone not Italian.

307
00:47:23,808 --> 00:47:27,395
- Like the Embassy, or Interpol.
- Interpol? <scoffs>

308
00:47:27,687 --> 00:47:30,064
I'm an American citizen.

309
00:47:30,690 --> 00:47:32,858
- What does that mean?
- I do not know.

310
00:47:32,858 --> 00:47:35,569
But I was involved in something here and no offense,
this is not a local issue.

311
00:47:37,530 --> 00:47:39,573
What is it you think you're involved in?

312
00:47:44,203 --> 00:47:48,416
It all started when I met a woman
on the train from Paris

313
00:47:48,999 --> 00:47:51,502
- This already good!
- No, no.

314
00:47:51,752 --> 00:47:53,379
She took me to her hotel.

315
00:47:53,629 --> 00:47:54,964
- Ah, wonderful!
- No, no.

316
00:47:55,172 --> 00:47:58,467
...she's involved with another man, I think she's in love...

317
00:47:59,510 --> 00:48:02,638
- Sorry to hear that
- I know

318
00:48:04,056 --> 00:48:04,849
...Anyway

319
00:48:05,975 --> 00:48:11,397
This man, whatever his story is.
Some people are obviously trying to kill him.

320
00:48:13,691 --> 00:48:16,986
- How do you know this?
- Because they tried to kill me.

321
00:48:18,612 --> 00:48:20,865
- They tried to kill you?
- Yes!

322
00:48:20,865 --> 00:48:24,827
Because they must have thought that I was him.

323
00:48:30,708 --> 00:48:33,836
- I like you Mr. Tupelo
- I like you too, sir

324
00:48:35,921 --> 00:48:38,591
But surely you understand how strange this all sounds.

325
00:48:43,804 --> 00:48:44,722
Come with me

326
00:48:53,647 --> 00:48:54,607
Where are you taking me?

327
00:49:00,446 --> 00:49:02,156
Oh!  You're going to lock me in there?

328
00:49:09,747 --> 00:49:14,001
Please don't do this.
Sir, I've done nothing wrong

329
00:49:17,254 --> 00:49:19,965
- Please!
- It's only until I check some facts

330
00:49:26,055 --> 00:49:26,681
Hi.

331
00:49:39,777 --> 00:49:42,697
Your facts checked out.
We have to leave.

332
00:49:44,865 --> 00:49:48,119
- You're not safe here
- I don't understand

333
00:49:49,578 --> 00:49:51,163
This has to look right.

334
00:49:54,625 --> 00:49:55,418
Come on

335
00:49:59,005 --> 00:50:01,340
The man you're talking about is
called Alexander Pierce

336
00:50:02,258 --> 00:50:04,427
...who stole big money from a gangster.

337
00:50:05,511 --> 00:50:07,013
They came to Venice to find him

338
00:50:08,681 --> 00:50:09,932
They think you are him

339
00:50:11,350 --> 00:50:16,647
They placed a... how do you say... bounty on your head.

340
00:50:19,025 --> 00:50:20,359
That's why you're not safe.

341
00:50:29,702 --> 00:50:30,661
Wait here for a moment

342
00:50:56,562 --> 00:50:58,147
You've come to buy a key?

343
00:51:10,993 --> 00:51:12,912
Brand new bills, I appreciate it

344
00:51:22,672 --> 00:51:23,798
You think we cheat you?

345
00:51:23,798 --> 00:51:26,217
Of course not, I just enjoy counting

346
00:51:35,893 --> 00:51:39,689
Well, gentlemen, Alexander Pierce is all yours.

347
00:51:49,281 --> 00:51:50,157
Do not shoot him!

348
00:52:11,178 --> 00:52:12,054
I think we lost them!

349
00:52:14,140 --> 00:52:15,599
I'd really like to take these off!

350
00:52:16,684 --> 00:52:18,436
We have to wait until we get to open waters

351
00:55:24,914 --> 00:55:27,958
It suits you perfectly, sir
You have a wonderful figure.

352
00:55:29,335 --> 00:55:34,507
- You think it's a little loose?
- No, it's of the utmost magnificence

353
00:55:42,223 --> 00:55:44,058
Fourteen red, bet made.

354
00:55:47,019 --> 00:55:47,436
Wager, sir?

355
00:55:50,272 --> 00:55:50,856
Forty-two red

356
00:55:54,860 --> 00:55:57,029
- They're back.
- Yeah, bring them in.

357
00:55:58,364 --> 00:56:00,741
- I'll come back tomorrow?
- No, no, no, stay.

358
00:56:11,043 --> 00:56:12,545
We tried everything, sir

359
00:56:14,380 --> 00:56:17,216
- But he got away.
- So I heard, so I heard.

360
00:56:18,592 --> 00:56:23,222
They're referring to the young man who
stole $2.3 billion dollars from me.

361
00:56:26,475 --> 00:56:29,729
You know, I worked very hard for years so I wouldn't have to

362
00:56:29,729 --> 00:56:33,607
do the dirty work any more. No more chasing traitors

363
00:56:34,316 --> 00:56:35,651
...No more killing

364
00:56:37,987 --> 00:56:41,866
Now I employ people
to do those things for me

365
00:56:43,200 --> 00:56:45,786
Except that you don't!

366
00:57:23,949 --> 00:57:27,578
- Does it look alright?
- Yes!

367
00:57:28,913 --> 00:57:31,791
- Like always.
- What's always?

368
00:57:33,751 --> 00:57:34,543
Very good.

369
00:57:37,296 --> 00:57:39,715
Yes, I think it looks alright!

370
00:57:55,314 --> 00:57:56,899
Huh, so that's how you pick a lock.

371
00:57:57,650 --> 00:57:58,984
How do you know how to do that?

372
00:58:03,572 --> 00:58:06,909
Where's the owner of this boat? Bottom of a canal?

373
00:58:07,910 --> 00:58:10,079
Sitting at a cafe with a pocketful of Euros

374
00:58:13,666 --> 00:58:17,670
Why is this happening?
Why is everyone trying to kill me?

375
00:58:20,381 --> 00:58:22,091
Because I kissed you.

376
00:58:29,849 --> 00:58:31,851
Do I look that much like him?

377
00:58:35,938 --> 00:58:38,607
I am sorry I got you involved in all this.

378
00:58:39,233 --> 00:58:40,943
Why are you involved in all this?

379
00:58:43,779 --> 00:58:48,075
- Because I'm in love with him.
- Really? I'm not.

380
00:58:49,368 --> 00:58:51,954
...Seriously, help me understand why?

381
00:58:52,371 --> 00:58:54,874
I honestly didn't think he would let it go this far.

382
00:58:55,458 --> 00:58:57,209
I didn't think he would let Shaw get to you.

383
00:58:58,044 --> 00:59:01,714
Shaw - that's the man who Pierce stole from?

384
00:59:03,174 --> 00:59:07,136
Reginald Shaw. Alexander used to be his private banker.

385
00:59:09,764 --> 00:59:14,560
- I thought he was Russian or something like that.
- He surrounds himself with the Russians.

386
00:59:14,977 --> 00:59:17,021
But he's as English as Alex and I.

387
00:59:19,106 --> 00:59:20,232
Give me your hand

388
00:59:21,484 --> 00:59:26,322
Now he owns most of the casinos and brothels
from here to Novus Brusk

389
00:59:28,783 --> 00:59:32,787
Once, he bragged to Alexander that he had every man killed

390
00:59:33,079 --> 00:59:35,039
his wife had slept with before she met him.

391
00:59:36,290 --> 00:59:39,502
And when he found out how many there had been... he killed her too.

392
00:59:41,754 --> 00:59:42,546
There you are.

393
00:59:46,634 --> 00:59:49,303
What made Pierce think he could take on a guy like that?

394
00:59:51,639 --> 00:59:52,682
It's just who he is.

395
00:59:59,980 --> 01:00:02,066
Could you ever feel like that about someone like me?

396
01:00:06,946 --> 01:00:12,159
I don't regret it, you know. Kissing you.

397
01:00:15,371 --> 01:00:19,542
I have to go check the, umm... the thing...

398
01:00:41,522 --> 01:00:42,481
Where are we going?

399
01:01:04,211 --> 01:01:05,087
The airport?

400
01:01:06,297 --> 01:01:08,257
- Where are we going?
- You'll see.

401
01:01:12,845 --> 01:01:14,347
Tie us up, would you?

402
01:01:30,321 --> 01:01:32,490
I wish we'd met in another life, Frank.

403
01:01:37,078 --> 01:01:39,914
Take the next flight back to America,
you'll find what you need in the bag.

404
01:01:42,958 --> 01:01:43,793
Be safe.

405
01:02:08,317 --> 01:02:09,610
But I'm in love with you...

406
01:03:32,818 --> 01:03:39,325
Agent Elise Clifton-Ward.
Identification number "M, F, S, 98495, G"

407
01:03:50,503 --> 01:03:51,462
<b><font color="green"size="30"> Clearance Authorization Approved </ b></b>

408
01:04:31,836 --> 01:04:33,504
Well, you've certainly blown your cover now.

409
01:04:34,296 --> 01:04:35,589
I'm ready to give you Pierce.

410
01:04:49,520 --> 01:04:52,356
You're ready to give me Pierce?

411
01:04:54,442 --> 01:04:55,484
Well that's interesting.

412
01:04:55,484 --> 01:04:58,946
So you're aren't here to beg me to lift your suspension?

413
01:05:00,072 --> 01:05:02,324
You've actually come to do your job?

414
01:05:03,534 --> 01:05:07,163
Allow me to ask.
Why now?

415
01:05:11,500 --> 01:05:13,461
You live with a man for an entire year.

416
01:05:13,461 --> 01:05:17,381
During which time, we don't get one single useable photograph.

417
01:05:18,883 --> 01:05:21,052
Now you're ready to give him up?

418
01:05:24,972 --> 01:05:27,558
It's because of that tourist, isn't it?

419
01:05:29,894 --> 01:05:32,396
I want to put an end to this
before someone gets killed.

420
01:05:44,658 --> 01:05:47,244
...I wish I could understand your choice in men.

421
01:05:49,497 --> 01:05:50,956
...The fugitive thief?

422
01:05:52,458 --> 01:05:55,127
Well, that's exciting, perhaps

423
01:05:56,045 --> 01:06:00,883
But a school teacher from Wisconsin?

424
01:06:02,468 --> 01:06:05,680
Who'd have thought your tastes were so provincial?

425
01:06:07,139 --> 01:06:11,060
- Do you want Pierce or not?
- Yes

426
01:06:13,145 --> 01:06:15,481
I'm meeting him at a ball. Tonight.

427
01:06:17,441 --> 01:06:19,819
You know you'll have to wear a wire?

428
01:07:01,944 --> 01:07:03,362
Hello Madam

429
01:07:35,895 --> 01:07:37,855
"She's moving toward the southeast corner"

430
01:07:48,407 --> 01:07:49,533
Where've you been?

431
01:07:52,286 --> 01:07:54,038
I thought you'd never get here.

432
01:07:55,664 --> 01:07:56,832
Really?

433
01:07:58,167 --> 01:07:59,335
"So tell me"

434
01:08:00,836 --> 01:08:02,254
Is that our man?

435
01:08:03,714 --> 01:08:05,508
How could you be so sure I was coming?

436
01:08:07,176 --> 01:08:08,302
I just knew it.

437
01:08:10,262 --> 01:08:13,182
Fate wouldn't bring me to an evening like this with no reason.

438
01:08:14,392 --> 01:08:17,228
As soon as you walked in, I knew what the reason was.

439
01:08:21,190 --> 01:08:24,193
- No?
- No

440
01:08:30,241 --> 01:08:35,454
"Count Philipe Organza, land owner, big reputation as a swordsman"

441
01:08:36,122 --> 01:08:38,374
Well, he won't be dueling tonight.

442
01:09:09,155 --> 01:09:09,989
Wait!

443
01:09:11,615 --> 01:09:14,035
Alexander!
Excuse me.

444
01:09:14,285 --> 01:09:15,828
It's Pierce, he's here.

445
01:09:15,828 --> 01:09:18,789
He just left her an envelope.  Pull
up the footage, we have his face.

446
01:09:38,559 --> 01:09:40,436
I don't bloody believe this!

447
01:09:40,978 --> 01:09:42,855
Alright, get that moron out of here.

448
01:09:43,481 --> 01:09:46,025
You shouldn't be -
I can't, I'm sorry.

449
01:10:03,292 --> 01:10:05,252
Come on, you owe me a dance.

450
01:10:17,640 --> 01:10:18,766
You shouldn't be here.

451
01:10:19,600 --> 01:10:22,603
No, Elise.  This is the only
place on earth I should be.

452
01:10:30,611 --> 01:10:32,154
How did you get in here?

453
01:10:32,488 --> 01:10:34,240
I told the doorman, you're my wife

454
01:10:34,240 --> 01:10:35,825
and I wanted to keep an eye on you.

455
01:10:36,075 --> 01:10:37,743
Italians are big on that kinda thing

456
01:10:40,746 --> 01:10:42,581
- Leave.
- No.

457
01:10:49,338 --> 01:10:52,299
Do you like the suit?
You paid for it.

458
01:10:55,428 --> 01:10:58,014
I've been thinking about your friend Pierce, and his plan.

459
01:10:58,806 --> 01:11:02,685
So far, I'm thinking it hasn't worked out for him.

460
01:11:03,185 --> 01:11:04,228
No?

461
01:11:04,645 --> 01:11:07,690
No, take that gangster guy.

462
01:11:08,024 --> 01:11:10,317
- Shaw?
- Yeah, Shaw.

463
01:11:10,901 --> 01:11:14,864
I don't believe that Pierce was prepared for him
being here.  The whole chase.

464
01:11:16,907 --> 01:11:18,993
Will you please leave?

465
01:11:22,246 --> 01:11:23,998
You're kinda worried about me, aren't you?

466
01:11:24,206 --> 01:11:25,041
Yes.

467
01:11:25,666 --> 01:11:27,168
And I'm worried about you

468
01:11:32,214 --> 01:11:33,758
And I'm not leaving without you

469
01:11:36,469 --> 01:11:40,890
You were part of the plan.
You were useful, that's all.

470
01:11:42,892 --> 01:11:46,103
Why do you think, I saw you on the
train and my heart stopped?

471
01:11:47,521 --> 01:11:48,773
Leave.

472
01:12:03,704 --> 01:12:04,789
This way please.

473
01:12:05,748 --> 01:12:07,375
Excuse me sir, I think you've made a mista--

474
01:12:30,106 --> 01:12:32,942
"Fondamenta San Giacomo 23, Tonight"

475
01:12:35,945 --> 01:12:37,321
What's it say?

476
01:12:42,493 --> 01:12:44,370
What's it say?

477
01:12:57,425 --> 01:12:58,884
Ms. Ward's boarding the boat.

478
01:13:01,053 --> 01:13:04,348
"It looks like they've called up her boat, what should I do?"

479
01:13:05,391 --> 01:13:08,477
She may just be playing with us, let's wait.

480
01:13:13,774 --> 01:13:16,110
Fondamenta San Giacomo 23, please

481
01:13:16,944 --> 01:13:19,071
Okay, good.  We have the address.

482
01:13:19,530 --> 01:13:21,032
I'm going to follow her on the boat.

483
01:13:21,449 --> 01:13:23,617
I want snipers on all surrounding roofs

484
01:13:23,951 --> 01:13:25,619
and if you get a visual on Pierce first, call.

485
01:13:51,604 --> 01:13:52,605
The Commissioner wants a report.

486
01:14:10,498 --> 01:14:11,290
Hello?

487
01:14:13,334 --> 01:14:14,710
Let's have a little fun with him

488
01:14:15,670 --> 01:14:17,254
Please?  (speaking spanish)

489
01:14:21,592 --> 01:14:23,886
Who are you people?
Where are we going?

490
01:14:25,388 --> 01:14:29,934
Well, I don't know, Alexander. Where are we going?

491
01:14:31,519 --> 01:14:35,398
I'm not Alexander, my name's Frank Tupelo.

492
01:14:35,981 --> 01:14:38,150
I'm an American citizen and I have rights

493
01:14:38,150 --> 01:14:40,653
I don't care what you call yourself these days

494
01:14:41,028 --> 01:14:43,989
Your name's Alexander Pierce and you have no rights

495
01:14:44,657 --> 01:14:48,494
Not until you pay us 744 million pounds back taxes

496
01:14:49,745 --> 01:14:52,081
Seven hundred and forty-four million?

497
01:14:52,081 --> 01:14:54,834
Looks like someone else is following our target.

498
01:14:59,380 --> 01:15:04,135
Reginald Shaw.
Well, this could be fun.

499
01:15:04,510 --> 01:15:06,053
Alright, stay close but not too close

500
01:15:06,053 --> 01:15:08,389
- And get the office to send me an interpreter.
- Right.

501
01:15:09,098 --> 01:15:12,309
Yes, 744 million

502
01:15:13,269 --> 01:15:16,856
You didn't think we knew about that
bank account in Liechtenstein.

503
01:15:18,274 --> 01:15:19,400
I don't know what you are talking about

504
01:15:19,692 --> 01:15:20,317
Listen

505
01:15:22,194 --> 01:15:23,279
...You asshole.

506
01:15:25,364 --> 01:15:26,824
I know everything about you.

507
01:15:27,491 --> 01:15:29,285
I even know how much that face cost.

508
01:15:30,286 --> 01:15:32,580
24 million wired to a Brazilian surgeon

509
01:15:32,580 --> 01:15:34,040
from a numbered Swiss bank account.

510
01:15:34,040 --> 01:15:35,875
I haven't been able to prove it

511
01:15:36,792 --> 01:15:38,252
...But now I don't have to.

512
01:15:40,421 --> 01:15:43,132
...Because I just lock you in a box in the basement

513
01:15:43,132 --> 01:15:45,259
Until you tell me where the money is.

514
01:15:56,812 --> 01:15:57,938
It's alright.

515
01:15:58,481 --> 01:15:59,940
It's alright, Frank.

516
01:16:01,567 --> 01:16:03,277
I know you're not Alexander Pierce

517
01:16:04,403 --> 01:16:07,448
But you know who you are?
You're a moron.

518
01:16:08,491 --> 01:16:12,703
And you're a moron that almost
ruined my ? million pound sting operation.

519
01:16:13,245 --> 01:16:14,121
Twice...

520
01:16:15,456 --> 01:16:17,917
So you're going to stay here until this is all over.

521
01:16:18,250 --> 01:16:21,253
Please, you can't do this
I haven't done anything

522
01:16:21,671 --> 01:16:22,963
I shouldn't be here.

523
01:16:23,631 --> 01:16:24,882
Know what I think?

524
01:16:25,716 --> 01:16:28,386
...I think that this is the one place on Earth

525
01:16:28,844 --> 01:16:30,680
You really should be.

526
01:16:35,768 --> 01:16:37,895
How was your night at the hotel?

527
01:16:39,563 --> 01:16:42,316
She's quite something, I'm sure.

528
01:16:42,316 --> 01:16:45,194
Target is about 200 yards away from destination.

529
01:16:45,194 --> 01:16:47,279
- We are matching speed.
- Good.

530
01:16:47,279 --> 01:16:48,614
But don't get too close.

531
01:16:49,782 --> 01:16:51,701
I don't want to scare Pierce off again.

532
01:17:01,752 --> 01:17:02,920
We're here.

533
01:17:09,260 --> 01:17:10,594
- Go ahead.
- Thank you.

534
01:17:10,886 --> 01:17:12,972
I won't be needing you any more this evening.

535
01:18:05,066 --> 01:18:06,275
Magnificent.

536
01:18:09,362 --> 01:18:13,783
I've never really understood the love that people devote to each other.

537
01:18:14,700 --> 01:18:17,078
Money, yes. Possessions, yes.

538
01:18:17,536 --> 01:18:22,333
But people are so unreliable, they sicken decay and die.

539
01:18:23,167 --> 01:18:26,712
But this, this is worth dying for.

540
01:18:45,189 --> 01:18:46,482
"...such good taste"

541
01:18:48,693 --> 01:18:49,568
We're live.

542
01:18:54,782 --> 01:18:55,950
Oh, yes, do sit down.

543
01:18:57,868 --> 01:18:58,703
When are you going in?

544
01:18:59,704 --> 01:19:01,205
You're welcome to stay and watch

545
01:19:01,539 --> 01:19:03,082
If you can keep your mouth shut

546
01:19:03,833 --> 01:19:06,085
"You know, Alexander was like a son to me"

547
01:19:06,627 --> 01:19:07,420
I loved him.

548
01:19:08,838 --> 01:19:13,259
That brilliant, playful, disrespectful young bastard.

549
01:19:15,803 --> 01:19:17,680
I even thought he and I were two of a kind.

550
01:19:19,515 --> 01:19:22,810
I took great pleasure never knowing
what the scamp would do next.

551
01:19:26,230 --> 01:19:31,152
Until one day, what he did next...
didn't give me any pleasure at all.

552
01:19:33,529 --> 01:19:35,865
...You know, in our quaint legal system

553
01:19:35,865 --> 01:19:37,283
...When a man sleeps with my wife

554
01:19:37,283 --> 01:19:40,578
...I kill him and her. Get away scot-free

555
01:19:41,203 --> 01:19:43,247
...Crime of passion as it was called

556
01:19:43,664 --> 01:19:46,709
But my passion extends to all the things I own

557
01:19:47,585 --> 01:19:51,172
They are me, they represent me.

558
01:19:52,173 --> 01:19:59,305
So if a man steals from me, I kill him
... I kill his wife, his children, his mother

559
01:19:59,930 --> 01:20:01,807
...I might even throw in the family doctor

560
01:20:01,807 --> 01:20:02,767
for good measure.

561
01:20:03,017 --> 01:20:06,520
For he has taken from me something for
which I have paid the infinite price.

562
01:20:08,189 --> 01:20:09,357
My Soul.

563
01:20:14,070 --> 01:20:16,989
That's something these idiots will never understand.

564
01:20:37,009 --> 01:20:38,511
He's not coming, is he?

565
01:20:41,305 --> 01:20:43,182
He sent you to get the money.

566
01:20:46,352 --> 01:20:52,149
So where is it?
Where's my money?

567
01:20:53,275 --> 01:20:57,029
- Where is the safe?
- I don't know.

568
01:20:57,613 --> 01:21:01,826
Where is the safe?

569
01:21:01,826 --> 01:21:03,327
I don't know.

570
01:21:03,327 --> 01:21:05,538
You don't know?

571
01:21:16,465 --> 01:21:18,801
Is it behind this bookcase here?

572
01:21:25,891 --> 01:21:28,602
...Or, perhaps

573
01:21:29,186 --> 01:21:30,312
...This one here

574
01:21:45,036 --> 01:21:47,872
- Where is the safe?
- ... I don't know, I haven't seen him si--

575
01:21:48,748 --> 01:21:50,124
Please, you have to do something

576
01:21:50,124 --> 01:21:51,542
Permission to fire?

577
01:21:51,542 --> 01:21:54,920
Hold your fire.  I repeat, hold your fire.
Not until Pierce shows himself.

578
01:21:56,380 --> 01:21:57,965
You're very beautiful, Elise.

579
01:21:57,965 --> 01:22:00,343
Try to combine it with a little intelligence.

580
01:22:00,968 --> 01:22:04,555
- And tell me where the safe is.
- If I knew it, I would tell you.

581
01:22:08,684 --> 01:22:09,894
In my opinion she knows nothing.

582
01:22:12,313 --> 01:22:14,815
You have to go in.
They're gonna kill her.

583
01:22:15,024 --> 01:22:17,318
- Where's my interpreter?
- They're going to kill her.

584
01:22:17,902 --> 01:22:20,738
- She can handle herself.
- She can handle herself?

585
01:22:21,989 --> 01:22:23,366
She's one of us.

586
01:22:24,325 --> 01:22:26,369
Expert in undercover operations.

587
01:22:27,328 --> 01:22:29,705
When I sent her to Russia to find Pierce

588
01:22:29,705 --> 01:22:31,707
She went dark.

589
01:22:31,999 --> 01:22:33,918
...I think she could never quite decide

590
01:22:33,918 --> 01:22:36,170
If she was with him, or with us.

591
01:22:36,712 --> 01:22:38,172
She's a good agent

592
01:22:38,381 --> 01:22:40,758
...Except that she invariably falls in love with any man

593
01:22:40,758 --> 01:22:43,010
That she spends longer than a train ride with.

594
01:22:45,763 --> 01:22:47,682
Commander Acheson, I'm the interpreter.

595
01:22:47,682 --> 01:22:49,016
Yes, go!

596
01:22:58,651 --> 01:23:00,695
If you could provide me with some context...

597
01:23:03,698 --> 01:23:05,616
...She really doesn't seem

598
01:23:07,076 --> 01:23:08,452
...To know where it is

599
01:23:08,869 --> 01:23:10,246
"We should go"

600
01:23:10,663 --> 01:23:12,248
We give it five more minutes

601
01:23:12,623 --> 01:23:18,587
If Parce doesn't show -
If Pierce doesn't show, we get rid of the woman and go.

602
01:23:22,258 --> 01:23:24,468
- Permission to engage?
- Negative.

603
01:23:24,885 --> 01:23:27,430
- Please!
- Not one more word from you.

604
01:23:31,600 --> 01:23:32,935
They won't kill her.

605
01:23:34,145 --> 01:23:35,604
Pierce will come.

606
01:23:36,647 --> 01:23:38,232
He has to come.

607
01:23:39,275 --> 01:23:40,943
Well alright, let's do it.

608
01:23:43,154 --> 01:23:43,988
No, knife.

609
01:23:47,241 --> 01:23:48,659
"Engaging target"

610
01:23:49,368 --> 01:23:53,831
- Negative, that is an order.
- Order the shot.

611
01:23:54,123 --> 01:23:56,709
Now if you don't tell me where the safe is

612
01:23:56,917 --> 01:24:00,629
I might be tempted to rearrange your face somewhat

613
01:24:10,973 --> 01:24:17,355
You'll find life is not quite so giving to an ugly woman.

614
01:24:26,447 --> 01:24:27,740
You really don't know, do you?

615
01:24:38,834 --> 01:24:39,585
There!

616
01:24:43,964 --> 01:24:45,383
Behind the medallion, there!

617
01:25:25,464 --> 01:25:26,298
Open it.

618
01:25:31,345 --> 01:25:32,888
There is movement in the courtyard

619
01:25:35,099 --> 01:25:36,392
Pierce, I knew it

620
01:25:41,814 --> 01:25:44,025
You know what, he does look a little like you

621
01:25:48,070 --> 01:25:49,155
No!

622
01:26:07,548 --> 01:26:08,466
Just try.

623
01:26:21,687 --> 01:26:23,189
Go on, press it.

624
01:26:26,359 --> 01:26:28,611
You may try one more time.

625
01:26:41,916 --> 01:26:43,042
Let her go!

626
01:26:45,378 --> 01:26:47,171
Oh, my God.

627
01:26:47,505 --> 01:26:50,174
- You let her leave and I'll open the safe.
- Stop right there.

628
01:26:52,593 --> 01:26:54,470
...Frank, what in hell?

629
01:26:54,720 --> 01:26:57,056
Please Elise let me handle this

630
01:26:58,683 --> 01:27:02,978
I'll say it again, let her go
I'll open the safe.

631
01:27:03,688 --> 01:27:07,733
- Who the hell are you?
- I'm Alexander Pierce.

632
01:27:08,651 --> 01:27:10,194
This is the man that was driving the boat

633
01:27:10,194 --> 01:27:13,364
- He is not Alexander Pierce.
- Elise, please.

634
01:27:13,364 --> 01:27:14,990
What the hell are you doing?

635
01:27:14,990 --> 01:27:16,409
What the hell is he doing?

636
01:27:16,409 --> 01:27:18,244
"Permission to engage target?"

637
01:27:18,536 --> 01:27:20,037
Shut the hell up.

638
01:27:21,872 --> 01:27:27,044
Alexander, is it you?  Truly?

639
01:27:27,670 --> 01:27:28,796
Truly.

640
01:27:31,799 --> 01:27:33,175
Show me your teeth

641
01:27:35,511 --> 01:27:39,306
Alexander had crooked teeth
Stained from excessive smoking

642
01:27:39,849 --> 01:27:42,018
Braces. Electronic cigarettes.

643
01:27:42,685 --> 01:27:44,478
He had a higher forehead

644
01:27:45,938 --> 01:27:48,232
I had a migraine for two weeks after the remodel

645
01:27:49,734 --> 01:27:52,737
- You sound different
- Voice chip implant

646
01:27:52,987 --> 01:27:55,197
No, no, I mean the the way you speak

647
01:27:55,489 --> 01:27:58,784
Yes, that's right, Alexander was English
This man is American

648
01:28:01,662 --> 01:28:04,081
I've actually gotten so used to the American accent

649
01:28:04,081 --> 01:28:06,167
that I find it a tad difficult to go back

650
01:28:06,959 --> 01:28:10,254
That's pathetic, this man is not Alexander Pierce

651
01:28:11,380 --> 01:28:12,465
He's a tourist!

652
01:28:14,633 --> 01:28:15,676
A tourist?

653
01:28:15,926 --> 01:28:18,387
Someone I happened to sit next to on the train

654
01:28:19,889 --> 01:28:21,307
How would a tourist

655
01:28:21,807 --> 01:28:24,352
know that you killed every man your wife ever slept with?

656
01:28:24,560 --> 01:28:26,103
I told him that

657
01:28:26,103 --> 01:28:28,731
You told a tourist?

658
01:28:29,190 --> 01:28:31,609
Why would she do that?
It's absurd.

659
01:28:33,402 --> 01:28:37,198
Well, there's a simple way of finding out

660
01:28:40,868 --> 01:28:44,455
- Open the safe
- I've made you a deal

661
01:28:01,620 --> 01:28:02,079
...When she's gone

662
01:28:46,540 --> 01:28:46,999
What are you doing?

663
01:28:47,333 --> 01:28:48,751
...and I know she's safe

664
01:28:49,126 --> 01:28:50,044
...Then

665
01:28:51,045 --> 01:28:53,089
Well... I'll make you an even better deal

666
01:28:54,090 --> 01:28:55,466
Open the safe now...

667
01:28:56,300 --> 01:28:59,970
And I won't make you watch something
that you would never forget.

668
01:29:02,348 --> 01:29:03,224
Open it!

669
01:29:09,105 --> 01:29:10,064
I see

670
01:29:11,524 --> 01:29:12,733
Now you see?

671
01:29:30,668 --> 01:29:33,421
- ...Sir
- I know him, he'll come for her

672
01:29:35,006 --> 01:29:36,257
I know him

673
01:29:36,507 --> 01:29:37,842
He won't give her up now

674
01:29:38,092 --> 01:29:39,301
"We must engage."

675
01:29:39,301 --> 01:29:42,263
"Permission to engage, sir?"

676
01:29:43,639 --> 01:29:44,890
Sir...

677
01:29:50,563 --> 01:29:52,815
I love you

678
01:30:16,797 --> 01:30:17,882
He'll come for her

679
01:30:19,050 --> 01:30:20,468
He'll come for her,
he doesn't make se-

680
01:30:21,594 --> 01:30:24,138
This is Chief Inspector Jones, permission granted!

681
01:30:25,848 --> 01:30:26,640
Fire!

682
01:31:28,327 --> 01:31:30,996
- Are you alright?
- Yes.

683
01:31:31,997 --> 01:31:34,166
Agent Ward, your suspension's lifted

684
01:31:35,167 --> 01:31:36,252
Thank you, sir

685
01:31:36,252 --> 01:31:40,423
And your employment is terminated,
effective immediately.

686
01:31:41,132 --> 01:31:42,675
Thank you, sir

687
01:31:46,095 --> 01:31:48,180
"We got him, we got Alexander Pearce."

688
01:31:48,556 --> 01:31:49,306
Where?

689
01:31:49,640 --> 01:31:52,727
"On the vondameta, 300 meters south of your location."

690
01:32:11,787 --> 01:32:13,289
So, you love me?

691
01:32:22,715 --> 01:32:23,924
I do.

692
01:32:26,635 --> 01:32:29,513
How do you feel about Alexander Pierce these days?

693
01:32:31,849 --> 01:32:34,894
I love him too, unfortunately

694
01:32:39,148 --> 01:32:40,941
I may have a solution for you

695
01:33:14,433 --> 01:33:16,143
Are you with me this time?

696
01:33:42,461 --> 01:33:43,254
Come on, let him up.

697
01:33:45,464 --> 01:33:46,424
I'm just a tourist.

698
01:33:50,594 --> 01:33:51,554
Just a tourist.

699
01:33:53,222 --> 01:33:55,349
He said I might get arrested at some point

700
01:33:55,474 --> 01:33:56,225
What?

701
01:33:56,642 --> 01:33:59,812
But that you'd have to let me go because you have nothing on me

702
01:34:00,396 --> 01:34:00,938
Who?

703
01:34:01,772 --> 01:34:03,357
The man who's been sending me these texts

704
01:34:04,108 --> 01:34:04,817
Texts?

705
01:34:06,068 --> 01:34:07,319
And the money, of course.

706
01:34:13,617 --> 01:34:16,746
So let me get this straight because I'm... a little confused

707
01:34:17,538 --> 01:34:19,957
You received money from a man you've never met before?

708
01:34:20,708 --> 01:34:25,338
Who sends you text messages telling you
just to show up somewhere

709
01:34:25,921 --> 01:34:26,797
Well...

710
01:34:30,926 --> 01:34:32,219
Not just anywhere...

711
01:34:44,398 --> 01:34:45,274
Clear!

712
01:35:07,797 --> 01:35:10,216
Seven hundred and fourty four million

713
01:35:18,599 --> 01:35:22,895
Inspector Acheson, this operation has been officially terminated.

714
01:35:23,521 --> 01:35:25,064
I'll expect your report on Monday.

715
01:35:25,356 --> 01:35:27,108
- Sir, listen
- We have our money, Acheson

716
01:35:27,108 --> 01:35:29,151
But we don't have Pierce.

717
01:35:30,027 --> 01:35:32,655
The man is a criminal wanted in 14 countries

718
01:35:33,614 --> 01:35:36,659
But what is it he did?  Really?

719
01:35:37,034 --> 01:35:40,955
He stole the money from a gangster. A dead gangster.

720
01:35:41,288 --> 01:35:43,040
And he has good taste in women.

721
01:35:44,542 --> 01:35:46,919
I can't say I don't wish him well.

722
01:36:27,251 --> 01:36:30,004
Twenty million dollars on plastic surgery...

723
01:36:30,755 --> 01:36:32,840
And that's the face you choose?

724
01:36:33,424 --> 01:36:36,594
- Do you not like it?
- It'll do.

725
01:37:20,554 --> 01:37:22,890

